## Model card (as curated in `meta.json`, not independently confirmed)

- **Name:** Gemini 3.1 Flash
- **Curated claim:** "Google's efficient 3.1 Flash model, balancing speed, capability, and cost." Context "1,048,576 (1M)"; modalities "Text, image, audio, PDF in; text out"; free tier on Google AI Studio + OpenCode Zen.
- **Provider / access:** not resolvable to a live GA chat endpoint (see findings below).
- **IDs:** curated `google/gemini-3.1-flash`; no matching OpenRouter / Vertex / AI-Studio chat ID found.

### Raw benchmarks found

> Exhausted sources on 2026-10-02. There is **no distinct, benchmarked "Gemini 3.1 Flash" text/chat model**:
> - **BenchLM** has no `gemini-3-1-flash` page (404) — it carries `gemini-3-1-flash-lite` (#86, 47.46) and `gemini-3-1-pro`, but no base "3.1 Flash".
> - **benchmarklist** `google-gemini-3.1-flash` returns 404.
> - The definitive FelloAI Gemini-generation lineup table lists the 3.x chat tiers as **3 Pro (Nov 2025), 3 Flash (Dec 2025), 3.1 Pro (Feb 2026), 3.1 Flash-Lite (Mar 2026), 3.5 Flash (May 2026), 3.5 Flash-Lite (Jul 2026)** — no "3.1 Flash" base.
> - The ai-toolbox "3.1 Pro vs Flash vs Flash-Lite" comparison describes the mid tier of that generation as **Gemini 3 Flash** (SWE-Bench Verified 78.0%), *not* a "3.1 Flash".
> - **OpenRouter** exposes `google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite`, `google/gemini-3-flash-preview`, `google/gemini-3.5-flash` — the only "3.1 Flash" surface is a separate **"Gemini 3.1 Flash Image"** (an image-generation model, different modality/task), never a scored chat model.
>
> Net: Reasoning (GPQA/HLE/LCR), Coding (SWE-bench/LiveCodeBench), and Context/retrieval each have **zero verified rows for this exact model** — because the model itself does not appear to exist as a measurable text/chat product. Every candidate number found belongs to a *sibling* (Gemini 3 Flash, 3.1 Pro, 3.1 Flash-Lite, or 3.1 Flash Image), and cross-variant borrowing is disallowed.

